[00:19.71]Once I was seven years old, my momma told me
[00:24.32]Go make yourself some friends or you'll be lonely
[00:27.87]Once I was seven years old

[00:35.90]It was a big, big world, but we thought we were bigger
[00:40.45]Pushing each other to the limits, we were learning quicker
[00:44.33]By eleven, smoking herb and drinking burning liquor
[00:48.31]Never rich, so we were out to make that steady figure

[00:52.36]Once I was eleven years old, my daddy told me
[00:56.22]Go get yourself a wife or you'll be lonely
[01:00.01]Once I was eleven years old

[01:08.46]I always had that dream like my daddy before me
[01:11.98]So I started writing songs, I started writing stories
[01:16.29]Something about that glory just always seemed to bore me
[01:20.16]'Cause only those I really love will ever really know me

[01:24.23]Once I was twenty years old, my story got told
[01:28.62]Before the morning sun, when life was lonely
[01:32.18]Once I was twenty years old

[01:40.25]I only see my goals, I don't believe in failure
